work_packages.description:
Goal: implement the @MainActor @Observable state layer behind the exact public API in DESIGN.md §4.10, depending ONLY on BranchBoxKit. Spec: §8 (8.1-8.6), D-16, D-17, D-18 and D-22, and the BranchBoxStoresTests row in §13.1.

1. AppModel.start():
   - bootstrap via BackendBootstrapping (EnvironmentStore.backendState);
   - run LegacyDefaultsMigration: import branchbox.workspace (only if backend.resolveProject succeeds; drop /workspaces/milestone2) and branchbox.promptHistory; delete branchbox.transportPreference, branchbox.teardown.force, branchbox.teardown.deleteBranch, branchbox.teardown.completeSpec and branchbox.devcontainerStrategy;
   - load ProjectsRepository (~/Library/Application Support/BranchBox/projects.json, {version:1, projects:[{root, displayName, addedAt, lastOpenedAt, pinned, collapsed}]}, atomic write, injectable directory);
   - validate roots (rootExists);
   - start watchers and timers.
   post(intent) sets pendingIntent and bumps intentToken; takePendingIntent clears it. backend() throws the unavailable error. prepareForTermination: operations.cancelAll() then bootstrapper.terminateAllProcesses(), bounded 10 s.
2. EnvironmentStore: rebootstrap() after settings changes (no relaunch); recaptureEnvironment; runDoctor; supports(capability).
3. ProjectsStore.add(folder:) → backend.resolveProject → AddProjectOutcome:
   - normalization note: 'This is a feature worktree of …/main; adding …/main instead';
   - duplicates by canonical path → alreadyPresent;
   - not initialized → needsInit;
   - errors → refused.
   Order: pinned, then lastOpenedAt desc. remove never deletes files. relocate and setPinned are supported.
4. ProjectStore.refresh(reason):
   - single-flight: an in-flight refresh sets rerun and returns; exactly one more pass runs. NEVER cancel-and-restart.
   - a generation guard drops stale results;
   - failures keep the last good features (.failed(error, lastGood:));
   - ListLimiter allows ≤ 2 concurrent listFeatures across projects;
   - features are sorted attention-first (Remediation-like attention computed with a local helper, since Planning lands in SW-3 in parallel), then updatedAt desc;
   - strays and droppedRecords are populated;
   - includeRemoved triggers a refresh with --all;
   - reloadConfig and reloadDetect use the backend.
5. RegistryWatcher: FSEvents on <root>/.branchbox with kFSEventStreamCreateFlagFileEvents|NoDefer, 0.2 s latency, 300 ms debounce. Port from $SP/design/arch-incremental/fsspike/main.swift. If .branchbox doesn't exist there is no watcher; start it after initProject completes.
6. RefreshCoordinator:
   - appDidBecomeActive → refresh projects whose data is > 5 s old;
   - selected-project timer (settings.selectedProjectRefresh) only while the app is active;
   - all-projects timer (settings.otherProjectsRefresh) regardless of activation;
   - injectable clock for tests.
7. OperationStore + ActionDispatcher:
   - dispatch(context): compute kind and target (§4.10 OperationKind flags), admission, OperationRecord; run the work in a Task capturing `try backend()`.
   - Progress flows ProgressSink → AsyncStream continuation → ONE MainActor consumer (ordered). EventBatcher applies log lines every 100 ms (≤ 10 invalidations/s). LogBuffer ring ≤ 10,000 lines. LogArchive streams the full redacted log to ~/Library/Logs/BranchBox/operations/<ISO>-<kind>-<feature>-<id>.log, retention settings.logRetention.
   - Map results to OperationResult and states (succeededWithWarnings when warnings exist; partial for TeardownOutcome.branch .deleteFailed, or a prune with failed/refused rows).
   - ALWAYS call requestRefresh(.afterOperation) on success, failure and cancel.
   - Notify via Notifier (UserNote) when the op took > 10 s or failed and settings allow. The app-active check is supplied by an injected closure that SW-4 wires.
   - perform(recovery) handles .retry(context) → dispatch; other recoveries return nil (UI-only).
   - title(for:) returns e.g. 'Starting oauth' or 'Tearing down beta'.
   Admission (D-16):
   - one mutating op per feature; exec is always allowed;
   - project-wide kinds are exclusive with all mutating ops in the project;
   - WITHOUT the registry-lock capability, every writesRegistry kind in a project runs FIFO via MutationQueue with state .queued(behind: <title>) (this includes syncDevcontainers, tunnel and config);
   - reads are never blocked.
   Prune: one record that runs PruneSelection rows sequentially, emits .phase(.item(i, of: n, name)), records PruneRowOutcome per row, skips and continues on refusal, and stops between rows on cancel.
   cancel(id) cancels the Task (the runner escalates). The UI confirms before calling it.
8. AppSettings: UserDefaults-backed properties per §4.10. defaultsForCurrentProcess() returns .standard when Bundle.main.bundleURL.pathExtension == "app", else UserDefaults(suiteName: "dev.branchbox.app.dev"). backendSettings maps agentChoice to a command (claude/codex/custom) plus a name.
9. Notifier contract stays as defined. NoopNotifier is used when isAvailable is false.
10. PreviewBackend: extend scenarios as needed (interrupted setup, strays, refusals with plan, legacy vs contract identity) and keep the call log.

Tests (Swift Testing, @MainActor, PreviewBackend plus an injected clock):
- three overlapping refreshes → exactly 2 listFeatures calls; the stale generation is dropped;
- a failed load keeps the last good data;
- selection lookup is nil after removal;
- refresh after success, failure and cancel;
- per-feature exclusivity;
- FIFO for registry writers (start + sync + tunnel) without .registryLock vs concurrent with it;
- project-wide exclusivity;
- prune skip-and-continue and stop-between-rows;
- 2,000 lines → ≤ 25 store mutations;
- events stay in order;
- legacy migration;
- intent token;
- FSEvents temp-dir test (in-place truncate+write and atomic rename within 2 s);
- ListLimiter;
- Notifier unavailable under xctest;
- projects.json round-trip and ordering.

changelog.d/sw-2.md.

Goal: the pure, UI-free planning layer (graft) plus the shared SwiftUI kit and presentation that wave-3 screens compose. Spec: DESIGN.md §4.9 (exact API), §9 (vocabulary, state catalogue, §9.1 remediation table, §9.4 error presentation), D-11 and §6.5.

1. Kit/Planning, pure Swift with no I/O:
   - RecoveryPlanner.recoveries(for:after:). Recoveries appear ONLY for the matching refusal or partial:
     - .uncommittedChanges(files) after a teardown context → .retry(.teardown(request with DiscardConsent(userFiles: exactly those paths)), label 'Discard N changes and tear down…', destructive true, confirmation listing the files);
     - .moduleFilesDirty(_, userChanges: []) → the same retry with an empty consent, labelled 'Discard BranchBox-generated files and tear down';
     - .moduleFilesDirty with user changes → the user-changes recovery;
     - .unmergedBranch → retry with .keep and retry with .forceDelete (destructive, confirmation lists the branch and commit count);
     - .worktreeLocked / .statusUnavailable / .worktreeNotFound → retry with forceRemoval true and .keep;
     - .worktreeExists after a start → retry start with reuse .existingWorktree(.fail);
     - .runtimePrerequisite sbx → .runInTerminal(["sbx","login"]);
     - cliNotFound / cliTooOld → .locateCLI and .copyCommand(brew …);
     - .partial(.unmergedBranch) → .retry(.deleteBranch(force: true));
     - commandFailed / decodeFailed / registryCorrupted → only .showLog and .openDoctor;
     - tunnel remove failure → .retry(.tunnelRemove(force: true)) with a second confirmation.
   - TeardownDraft:
     - defaults: config.deleteBranchByDefault ? .deleteIfMerged : .keep, but .keep when the branch exists unmerged; never preselect .forceDelete;
     - visibleBranchOptions adds .forceDelete only when unmerged;
     - blockingReason when .deleteIfMerged is chosen and the branch is unmerged;
     - pendingDiscardWarning when the plan has user changes;
     - makeRequest() ALWAYS returns discard nil and forceRemoval false.
   - PrunePlanner: rows for status != removed. Preselect the safe set: no user changes AND (merged OR policy keep), plus failed_retained / orphaned. defaultReason text for unselected rows. selection() builds TeardownRequests; dirty rows get per-row consent only via the sheet popover (SW-6).
   - StartDraft: promptLimit 2000; validation (slug valid, collisions vs existing records — registry duplicate is an error, removed is info, folder exists is an error unless reuse; keepRuntimeOnFailure only with sbx); makeRequest() returns nil when invalid and always sets an explicit runtime.
   - Remediation: attention() and actions() per the DESIGN §9.1 table, including setup interrupted, failed modules, folder missing, unknown status. Note degraded is unreachable for container (core defaults).
   - HostLaunchPlan:
     - editor by bundle id (com.microsoft.VSCode, com.todesktop.230313mzl4w4u92) or a custom app;
     - Dev Container URI `vscode-remote://dev-container+<hex(worktree)><workspace_folder>` (container only);
     - terminal script content `cd <quoted path> && exec <argv>`, properly single-quote escaped;
     - agent command resolution: project editor.default_agent → AgentChoice; optional prompt as the first argument;
     - devcontainer shell `docker exec -it -u <remoteUser> -w <remoteWorkspaceFolder> <containerId> bash -l`;
     - sbx terminal or agent → .disabled(reason) with copy command `sbx exec <runtime_id> bash`;
     - missing folder → disabled.
   - NameRules: slug and preview helpers shared by StartDraft.
2. App/Components (SwiftUI, macOS 14):
   - StatusBadge (icon plus text, never colour-only; port the layout from `git show v0.13.4:macos/Sources/BranchBoxApp/Views/MainAppView.swift` lines 124-137);
   - RuntimeBadge, ColorSwatch (8 pt, separator stroke, accessibilityHidden), ModuleChecklist, PortLinks;
   - FlowLayout (port from v0.13.4 FeatureDetailView.swift 156-218);
   - ResultCard: refusal, partial, failure and success-with-warnings; shows RecoveryPlanner actions through an `onRecovery: (RecoveryAction) -> Void` callback; destructive ones require a confirmationDialog showing the confirmation text; [Show Log] and [Copy diagnostic report];
   - ErrorBanner;
   - LogView: monospaced, selectable, level icons, timestamps toggle, auto-scroll pausing on scroll-up with 'Jump to Latest', warnings filter, find;
   - OperationRow and OperationProgressView: title, elapsed, phase, live log, [Run in Background] / [Stop] with the cancel confirmation copy per D-18, using the capabilities to choose the warning text;
   - EmptyStates: ContentUnavailableView variants for CLI not found, CLI too old, project missing, no features, feature gone;
   - CopyButton (HUD plus AccessibilityNotification.Announcement), AttentionBadge.
   - Every component has a #Preview using PreviewBackend data.
3. Presentation:
   - status label, symbol, tint and attention per DESIGN §9 (failed_retained → 'Failed (kept)'; unknown → raw value with underscores as spaces);
   - module summary '3 ok · 1 skipped · 0 failed';
   - tunnel labels (pending → Starting, active → Online, manual → Manual setup needed, disabled → Off);
   - relative dates via Date.FormatStyle (no shared mutable formatters);
   - BackendError → title and message per the §9.4 table;
   - DiagnosticReport: redacted Markdown with app version and SHA (Info.plist BranchBoxGitSHA if present), CLI path, source, version and capabilities, child PATH, redacted argv, exit/signal and the last 50 stderr lines.
4. Services:
   - HostLauncher executes HostLaunchPlan through NSWorkspace (open with app bundle id or path; URLs). It writes .command scripts at 0700 to ~/Library/Caches/BranchBox/launch/ and opens them with Terminal (iTerm or a custom template). It returns typed errors, never try?.
   - Pasteboard helper.

Tests:
- Kit Planning tests per the DESIGN §13.1 Planning row;
- PresentationTests: every FeatureStatus has a distinct non-empty label and symbol; the error presentation table; the module summary.

changelog.d/sw-3.md.

Goal: teardown never deletes user work without --force or --discard-changes, refuses before mutating anything, treats BranchBox's own files as not dirty, refuses non-interactive unmerged deletes up front, and deletes the branch actually recorded. Spec: DESIGN.md §10.2, §5.5 and §5.6, plus the core/CLI spec S1, S4, S5, C10a, C10b, C10c and C3. D-27: --force KEEPS implying -D when deleting, for compatibility.

1. core teardown_plan.rs:
   - the S4 classifier (rules R1-R7 exactly as in DESIGN §6.5) over `git status --porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all --no-renames --ignore-submodules=none`, with a ChangeContext trait so tests can use a fake;
   - a -z parser that handles spaces, quotes, ' -> ', unicode and NUL framing;
   - an 8 MiB cap; symlinks never followed; path-traversal guard; 2,000-entry truncation;
   - move is_module_managed_path (feature.rs:1975-2014) here for `area`;
   - pub(crate) const VSCODE_MANAGED_SETTINGS shared with setup_vscode_workspace (feature.rs:3155-3243);
   - build_teardown_plan producing TeardownPlan with blockers uncommitted_changes / unmerged_branch / worktree_locked / status_unavailable;
   - refusal_message() names the files (up to 10 in text, all in JSON) and both fixes;
   - CAPABILITIES = ["teardown-plan","teardown-discard-changes","teardown-unmerged-preflight"].
2. core feature.rs:
   - FeatureWorkflow::plan_teardown(&req, &opts) (read-only), teardown_with_options(req, opts), and teardown(req) delegating with TeardownOptions::legacy (the agent compiles unchanged), plus validate_host().
   - Branch resolution: explicit --branch-prefix, then the registry's branch_name, then the config prefix (C10c; replaces 1067-1069; move recorded_metadata up).
   - Replace 1094-1104 with plan blockers evaluated BEFORE any tunnel, module, spec, adapter or runtime step → Err(TeardownRefused).
   - Replace 1201-1229: unless discard/force, re-classify → new user dirt stops with changed_anything=true and completed_steps, keeping the worktree and registry entry. Otherwise `git worktree remove --force` (level 1), or `-f -f` only under --force.
   - remove_dir_all ONLY under --force, keeping the existing warning strings verbatim. A non-force git failure gives TeardownRefused{worktree_removal_failed{cause}}.
   - A missing branch is skipped with a warning.
   - record_teardown only when the worktree is gone or was missing.
   - remove_baseline after removal.
   - handle_spec_on_teardown returns Option<PreservedFile>.
   - TeardownSummary additive fields: branch_action, branch_delete_error, discarded_changes, preserved, registry_updated.
3. core git.rs:
   - status_entries (-z); worktree lock detection;
   - branch_merge_state(branch) with git branch -d semantics (upstream if configured and resolves, else HEAD; merged = merge-base --is-ancestor; ahead = rev-list --count; run from repo_root);
   - removal force levels.
4. S5 decision matrix (core spec table):
   - non-interactive (no TTY or --json) + delete + unmerged + no force flags → force_delete_unmerged_by_default ? -D : refuse BEFORE any change, naming --keep-branch / --force-delete-branch;
   - interactive behaviour unchanged, but the prompt's yes sets only force_delete_branch;
   - a -d failure after the preflight → exit 0, branch_deleted=false, branch_delete_error;
   - when --force causes -D of an unmerged branch, add the warning 'Force-deleted unmerged branch <b> (<n> commits); use --discard-changes to discard files without deleting unmerged commits'.
5. cli feature.rs:
   - FeatureTeardownArgs adds --discard-changes and --dry-run; accurate --force help.
   - run_teardown is rewritten around validate_host → plan_teardown. --dry-run renders the plan and exits 0 (text listing, or JSON per §5.5).
   - Branch decision, then the dirty decision. The interactive confirm sets only discard_changes.
   - teardown_with_options(req, {discard_changes: force||discard, require_mergeable_branch: true}).
   - Delete build_branch_name, local_branch_exists, local_branch_is_merged and the post-hoc bail (860-872); stop injecting the config prefix (839).
   - Text banner first line stays '⚠️  Detected devcontainer/compose changes inside <path>:' when module areas are involved (scripts/manual-cli-e2e.sh:951), else '⚠️  Detected uncommitted changes inside <path>:'. Use humanln!.
   - In JSON mode a refusal is the teardown_refused envelope with details {plan, changed_anything, completed_steps}.
   - commands::feature::CAPABILITIES = ["prune-json"].
6. C3 prune (feature.rs 215-246, 883-990):
   - --json and repeatable --feature;
   - per-candidate plan under prune's options;
   - text annotations of what will be lost;
   - dry-run / execute JSON per DESIGN §5.9;
   - confirmation_required in machine mode without --yes;
   - pass branch_prefix None;
   - keep the documented forced semantics.
7. Update existing tests:
   - feature.rs:7185 feature_teardown_prunes_stale_worktree_entries now asserts a refusal with files intact;
   - 7239 asserts the new variant with area devcontainer;
   - cli/tests/feature_commands.rs `--force` tests keep passing.
8. New tests:
   - cli/tests/teardown_safety.rs: BUG-04 regression (M README.md + ?? notes.txt, `teardown --keep-branch` → exit 1, both files named, files exist, list still active); the same with --json (one envelope, details.plan.changes.user has both); --discard-changes removes and deletes a merged branch with -d; --dry-run --json exits 0 with no FS change; the E4 scenario (fresh minimal feature in a repo without .gitignore, `teardown --json` with no flags) → exit 0 with the spec preserved in main backlog; a tracked .vscode/settings.json repo → OK, then editor.formatOnSave added → refused naming it; full mode with a committed devcontainer → OK, worktree edit → refused with area devcontainer; unmerged + default delete + non-TTY → exit 1 BEFORE removal (worktree and registry active); --keep-branch → exit 0 with the branch kept; --force-delete-branch → branch_action force_delete; custom prefix (start --branch-prefix spike; teardown without prefix) deletes spike/<n>; locked worktree refused then removed with --force; corrupted .git file → status_unavailable naming the git stderr; harness phrase on stdout in text mode.
   - cli/tests/prune_json.rs: dry-run lists candidates with plans; --yes --json results; --feature filters; machine mode without --yes gives confirmation_required.
   - git.rs unit tests: merged, unmerged ahead=1, upstream-pushed not merged into HEAD, missing branch, detached HEAD, and a branch checked out in a linked worktree (the '+' marker) treated correctly.
   - Fixtures under cli/tests/fixtures/contract/teardown/ via assert_fixture.
9. changelog.d/rs-2.md: Fixed (BUG-04, UX-13, DRIFT-07); Changed (non-interactive unmerged refusal happens before removal; non-force teardown no longer silently discards work, including for agent IPC); Added (--discard-changes, --dry-run, prune --json/--feature).

Do not edit scripts/manual-*.md or docs pages (DOC-1). If a harness expectation would change, record it in the changelog fragment.

Goal: the running app shell over the real CLI. SW-4 is also the integration owner of the shared layers in wave 3: Stores, Preview, Planning, Components, Presentation and Services. It makes only ADDITIVE changes there, and other wave-3 packages request changes from SW-4. Spec: DESIGN.md D-7, §8.7, §9 (scenes and menus table, Sidebar, EnvironmentGate, Menu bar, Quick Open), §11 (notifications, dev loop) and §4.11.

First PR, milestone M1 (within about 2 days of wave 3 starting):
- CompositionRoot builds AppSettings(defaults: .defaultsForCurrentProcess()), CLIBackendBootstrapper (from BranchBoxCLI), the Notifier (UserNotificationNotifier only if bundle id != nil && bundleURL.pathExtension == "app", else NoopNotifier), then AppModel. In DEBUG, BRANCHBOX_BACKEND=preview uses PreviewBootstrapper.
- MainWindow with a two-column NavigationSplitView, Sidebar with the real feature list, detail routed to FeatureDetailView / ProjectDetailView / WelcomeView stubs, and EnvironmentGate. A teardown dispatched via ActionDispatcher from the sidebar context menu ('Tear Down (keep branch)' debug item) proves the end-to-end slice.

Then:
1. Scenes (BranchBoxApp.swift):
   - Window("BranchBox", id: SceneID.main), defaultSize 1100×720, min 800×520, with .commands { AppCommands };
   - MenuBarExtra(isInserted: $settings.showMenuBarIcon) { MenuBarContent } label: { MenuBarLabel } with .menuBarExtraStyle(.menu);
   - Settings { AppSettingsView() };
   - WindowGroup("Run Command", id: SceneID.run, for: FeatureRef.self) { RunCommandWindow(feature: $0.wrappedValue) };
   - Window("Activity", id: SceneID.activity) { ActivityWindow() };
   - Window("Diagnostics", id: SceneID.diagnostics) { DiagnosticsWindow() }.
   All of them get .environment(model).
2. AppDelegate:
   - no activation at launch;
   - applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed = false;
   - applicationShouldHandleReopen → WindowOpener (a captured openWindow from MenuBarLabel; fallback NSApp.windows.first { identifier hasPrefix main }.makeKeyAndOrderFront);
   - applicationShouldTerminate: when operations.running is non-empty, return .terminateLater and show an NSAlert 'N operations are running. Quitting stops them and may leave partial state.' [Cancel and Quit] / [Keep Running]; Cancel and Quit awaits model.prepareForTermination(), then reply;
   - didBecomeActive → model.appDidBecomeActive();
   - wire the app-active closure for notification decisions.
3. PresentationRouter (@Observable, per window):
   - exactly ONE .sheet(item: $router.sheet, onDismiss: router.promoteNext);
   - consumes model.pendingIntent on .onChange(of: model.intentToken) and on appear;
   - maps WindowIntent → selection or SheetRoute;
   - while a sheet is up, further intents queue as `next` (never sheet-on-sheet);
   - SheetHost switches SheetRoute → the stub/screen views.
   Selection uses @SceneStorage("selection") with the JSON-encoded SidebarSelection.
4. Sidebar per DESIGN §9 Sidebar row:
   - a DisclosureGroup per project, with project rows and a context menu;
   - feature rows: swatch, name, StatusBadge, RuntimeBadge, Quick capsule, op spinner; double-click opens the editor via HostLauncher; context menu FeatureActionsMenu(feature:, style: .contextMenu);
   - stray rows labelled 'Unregistered worktree' that post .stray;
   - a provisional 'starting…' row while a start op runs;
   - 'Show removed (n)';
   - .searchable(placement: .sidebar);
   - loading, empty, error and stale states;
   - combined accessibility labels and identifiers sidebar.project.<id> / sidebar.feature.<p>.<n>.
   Toolbar: Start Feature, Refresh, an Activity button with a running-count badge that opens ActivityPopover (from SW-6, via SheetHost-free popover hosting), and an inspector toggle hosting ActivityInspector(target:).
5. EnvironmentGate: the ContentUnavailableView variants from Components plus the legacy-CLI banner text from DESIGN §9.
6. AppCommands: the menus and shortcuts in the DESIGN §9 table (⌘N replaces .newItem, ⌘O, ⌘R, ⌘K, ⌘⌫, ⌥⌘R, ⌃⌘E/T/A/O/R, ⌥⌘C, ⇧⌥⌘C, ⌥⌘I, ⇧⌘., ⌥⌘L). They target the key window via @FocusedValue (FocusedValues.swift); with no main window they post an intent and open it. Commands are disabled with .help reasons.
7. QuickOpenPalette: an overlay (not a sheet) with stable item ids, ↑↓/Return navigation, features × actions, projects and global commands. It posts an intent after closing.
8. Menu bar (.menu style) per the DESIGN §9 menu-bar row:
   - header summary;
   - blocking CLI item → openWindow(diagnostics);
   - last 3 operations;
   - per-project sections with ≤ 8 non-removed features, each a submenu FeatureActionsMenu(.menuBar);
   - Start Feature in <project>…;
   - global Start Feature… ⌘N, Open BranchBox, Refresh ⌘R, SettingsLink, Quit;
   - an 'Updated n s ago' line.
   Items that need a sheet call openWindow(id: main) + NSApp.activate() + model.post(intent). NO .sheet or .alert anywhere in MenuBar/. The label's states are idle, working (dot), attention (badge plus count) and blocked, with an accessibility label.
9. UserNotificationNotifier: lazy authorization; a delegate whose willPresent suppresses banners when frontmost (announcement plus in-window toast); category actions Show and Open in Editor; a click posts the intent; failures are soft.
10. scripts/macos-dev.sh:
   - builds debug (`swift build --package-path macos --product BranchBox`);
   - wraps it as macos/build/dev/BranchBox Dev.app (CFBundleIdentifier dev.branchbox.app.dev, LSMinimumSystemVersion 14.0, inline plist heredoc), ad-hoc signed with `codesign --force --sign - --options runtime`;
   - runs the inner binary in the foreground by default;
   - `--open` launches it via `open` (launchd environment).
11. RouterTests: a palette intent is presented only after dismissal; two consecutive intents never stack; an intent posted while closed is consumed on appear; the command enablement matrix.

changelog.d/sw-4.md.

Goal: everything shown for one feature. Spec: DESIGN.md §9 rows Feature detail, Feature actions and Run Command window; §9.1 remediation; §9.2 environment card; §9.3 sharing card. Keep the exact stub initializers from §4.11. Use only the AppModel / ActionDispatcher / Planning / Components APIs; request shared-layer additions from SW-4.

1. FeatureDetailView(feature:):
   - resolve `model.projects.project(feature.project)?.feature(named:)` on every render; nil → EmptyStates 'This feature no longer exists' with [Show Removed Features] (posts select plus includeRemoved);
   - title and subtitle; header (swatch, name, StatusBadge, RuntimeBadge, Quick, 'branch from base · created …');
   - toolbar: Editor split button (VS Code / Cursor / Open in Dev Container), Terminal, Launch Agent, Open URL menu, Run Command… (openWindow(id: run, value: feature)), and an overflow (Environment ▸, Sharing ▸, Copy ▸, Reveal, Tear Down… → model.post(.teardown));
   - HealthCallout from Remediation.actions → each action dispatches its OperationRequestContext, or posts an intent for teardown-type actions; buttons are disabled while operations.active(for: .feature) exists;
   - cards in a 2-column grid wider than 900 pt: Overview (live `git log -1` subject via a backend read is NOT available, so show last_commit's short SHA only and defer the subject; folder 'Missing' state), Open links (FeatureURLs; container runtime service info from backend.devcontainerStatus labelled 'inside container — open if forwarded'), Runtime, Environment, Sharing, Setup checklist (ModuleChecklist), Coding agent and prompt (default_agent status and detail; prompt seed with Show All popover, Copy, Launch with Prompt), Adapter warnings, PR card ('#n' or 'No pull request linked');
   - removed features: read-only with a removed_at banner and [Delete Branch…] when the branch exists (backend.listBranches) → .deleteBranch(force: false), with -D only after a confirmation listing commits.
2. FeatureActionsMenu(feature:, style:): the shared menu for the sidebar context menu, menu bar submenu and toolbar overflow. Items: Open in Editor/Terminal/Launch Agent (HostLaunchPlan via HostLauncher), Open URL ▸, Copy Branch/Path/Name, Reveal, the primary remediation item, Tear Down…, and (menuBar style) Show in BranchBox. Disabled items carry .help reasons (missing folder; sbx 'needs branchbox feature exec --interactive (planned)' with Copy Command). In menuBar style it must render as plain Buttons and Menus only (it lives in a .menu MenuBarExtra).
3. EnvironmentCard:
   - container: status from backend.devcontainerStatus (Running / Stopped / Not created / Unknown), refreshed on appear and after ops; [Start] → .devcontainer(.up(false, false)); [Stop] → .down(removeVolumes: false), with the volume option behind a confirmation; [Rebuild…] → confirmation → .up(removeExisting: true, buildNoCache: true); explanation line;
   - sbx: status from the record, Start Environment per §9.1, Stop and Rebuild disabled with a reason;
   - local-vm / in-guest read-only;
   - devcontainer_outdated → 'Config out of date' with [Update All Workspaces…] (posts .syncDevcontainers).
4. TunnelCard per §9.3: [Share via Tunnel] → .tunnelOpen; [Stop Sharing…] → confirmation → .tunnelRemove(force: false); a failure gives a ResultCard recovery for force with a second confirmation; manual instructions as a numbered list; tunnels-off note with [Project Settings…].
5. RunCommandWindow(feature:):
   - command field with per-feature history and per-project quick commands (AppSettings);
   - 'Run through shell' toggle (default on → ["/bin/sh","-lc",text]);
   - target picker Feature runtime / Dev container (container and running only);
   - Run ⌘↩ → .exec(ExecRequest), Stop ⌘. (with the cancel confirmation);
   - output from OperationResult.exec: segmented Output/Errors, exit-code badge (0 green, else red), duration, Copy/Save…, 32 MiB truncation note;
   - a non-zero exit is NOT an error alert;
   - [Open in Terminal Instead];
   - disabled for orphaned or removed features or when the CLI is missing.
6. Accessibility: every icon-only button has an accessibilityLabel; card titles use the .isHeader trait; identifiers feature.action.<verb>.
7. FeatureSurfaceTests (view-model level, PreviewBackend):
