Goal: the destructive and long-running flows, with the safety invariants enforced in the UI. Spec: DESIGN.md D-11, D-12, D-18, §6.5 (semantics), §9 rows Start Feature sheet, Teardown sheet, Prune sheet, Stray sheet and Activity, and §4.9 (TeardownDraft, PrunePlanner, StartDraft, RecoveryPlanner). Keep the stub initializers. Each sheet owns a value-type draft created per presentation and discarded on cancel (MAC-18). A sheet never presents another sheet: confirmations are .confirmationDialog inside the sheet, and chaining uses model.post.

1. StartFeatureSheet(project:prefill:):
   - project picker when ambiguous;
   - title/slug field with a 250 ms debounced backend.previewName ('Feature oauth · Branch feature/oauth · Folder …/oauth') and an 'Edit name' override;
   - collision checks via StartDraft.validationErrors (registry, removed, folder exists via FileManager, branch exists via listBranches);
   - searchable base picker from backend.listBranches (Current HEAD default);
   - runtime radio from EnvironmentStore.doctor (Container with Docker status; Docker Sandbox if sbx installed, with sign-in state and [Sign in…] → runInTerminal sbx login; Local VM disabled 'Linux with KVM only'; in-guest hidden; default from config runtime.provider, falling back with a note);
   - Full/Quick;
   - prompt TextEditor with counter and a hard cap of 2000, Recent prompts (AppSettings.promptHistory), and a default-prompt toggle (Quick only);
   - Advanced (remembered per project in AppSettings): branch prefix, skip modules (tunnel locked when tunnels are off), Reuse + devcontainer conflict policy, Keep sandbox on failure (sbx), Verbose;
   - footer: Copy as Command (backend.previewCommandLine), Cancel (Esc), Start (Return; label shows queued state).
   On Start → dispatch(.start); the sheet becomes OperationProgressView with Run in Background / Stop. The result (StartResultView) shows the RESOLVED work_feature, the checklist, warnings plus adapter warnings (with the stash warning text highlighted), skipped modules, links, and [Open in Editor] as default. It auto-launches the agent when config autoLaunchAgentTerminal is set. A failure gives a ResultCard with [Edit and Retry] and [Show Feature] if a partial entry appeared.
2. TeardownSheet(feature:preselect:):
   - on appear, backend.planTeardown(TeardownDraft request), shown with 'Checking for unsaved work…';
   - sections: user changes ('will be permanently deleted' with pendingDiscardWarning), generated (safe), preserved spec destination, unmerged commits (count; subjects are deferred if no backend API — show count and branch), runtime resources, active tunnel, folder already gone;
   - branch radio from TeardownDraft.visibleBranchOptions with an inline blockingReason; Force-delete requires a confirmationDialog listing the commit count;
   - complete spec only if a preserved spec exists;
   - footer: Copy as Command, Cancel (default focus), Tear Down (destructive, no Return).
   Tear Down → dispatch(.teardown(draft.makeRequest())) — FIRST ATTEMPT NEVER CARRIES DISCARD. On .refused / .partial, show the ResultCard IN THE SAME SHEET with RecoveryPlanner recoveries ('Discard N changes and tear down…' → confirmationDialog listing the files → model.actions.perform(recovery)). The result (TeardownResultView) shows worktree removed (verified), branch kept / deleted (by CLI or app) / delete failed with [Force-delete Branch…] only when unmerged, runtime cleanup verified / residue list with [Copy Cleanup Commands] (docker rm -f / docker volume rm, copied not run) / couldn't verify, module reports, warnings, and a red flag for 'removed manually after git removal failed'.
3. PruneSheet(project:):
   - rows from features with status != removed;
   - per-row planTeardown with bounded concurrency 4;
   - PrunePlanner preselection with [Select Safe] [All] [None];
   - batch branch policy Keep (default) / Delete if merged / Force-delete (confirmation listing rows);
   - checking a dirty row opens a popover 'Delete N uncommitted files in <f>?' → that row's request gets DiscardConsent(userFiles: those files) — the ONLY place consent is created outside RecoveryPlanner, and it is per-row explicit;
   - Prune → dispatch(.prune(selection));
   - per-row states, [Stop After Current];
   - PruneResultView: '5 torn down · 1 partial · 0 failed' with expandable rows;
   - empty: 'Nothing to prune'.
4. StrayWorktreeSheet(project:stray:): path, branch, dirty state (via planTeardown is N/A; use removeStray refusal); [Reveal], [Open in Terminal], [Remove Worktree…] → dispatch(.removeStray(discardChanges: false)); a refusal offers 'Discard N changes and remove' with a confirmation; option to delete the branch if merged.
5. Activity:
   - ActivityInspector(target:): operations for the target, newest first, rows expanding to OperationProgressView;
   - ActivityWindow: master-detail of all operations with filters by project and state, Reveal Log File, Copy diagnostic report;
   - ActivityPopover for the toolbar: running plus recent, [Show All] → openWindow(activity);
   - viewing a failed or partial record calls acknowledge();
   - Stop always shows the D-18 confirmation (legacy copy mentions the partial worktree and possible registry corruption).
6. FlowTests (PreviewBackend call log):
   - cancelling Start leaves no draft state for the next presentation;
   - a 2,001-char prompt blocks submit;
   - the start request never contains a title;
   - the teardown's first dispatch has discard == nil even when the plan lists user changes;
   - after a scripted .refused(.uncommittedChanges([notes.txt])) the recovery retry carries exactly [notes.txt];
   - an unmerged branch defaults to Keep and Delete-if-merged disables Tear Down;
   - prune with 3 rows where row 2 is refused reports row 2's cause and completes rows 1 and 3;
   - Stop presents a confirmation.

